OL,3,GNEWSAResidents could face second 8.99%
OL,4,Acouncil tax rise
OL,5,
OL,6,FResidents could face a second
OL,7,Fconsecutive council tax rise of 8.99%
OL,8,Fafter Shropshire Council was advised to
OL,9,Fseek another increase above the usual
OL,10,Flimit.
OL,12,FThe authority increased its share of
OL,13,Fbills by 8.99% in April after receiving
OL,14,Frare government permission to exceed
OL,15,Fthe normal cap on council tax rises.
OL,17,FA recently published finance report has
OL,18,Frecommended that council tax should be
OL,19,Fraised again "to the maximum possible
OL,20,Flevel" permitted by the government in
OL,21,F2027-28.
OL,23,APub: 20-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (W) NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,358,350,200,160,0,100
